},"487":{"id":"/configuration/init-command-77","page_id":"/configuration/init-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/configuration/init-command#skill-projecttoml-already-exists-use---force-to-overwrite","content":"**Cause**: a `skill-project.toml` is already present.\n**Solution**: pass `--force` to overwrite it, or remove the file first."},"488":{"id":"/configuration/init-command-78","page_id":"/configuration/init-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/configuration/init-command#project-level-init-requires---skills-dir","content":"**Cause**: `--yes` was used at a project root without a skills directory.\n**Solution**: add `--skills-dir <path>`, or drop `--yes` to be prompted."},"489":{"id":"/configuration/init-command-79","page_id":"/configuration/init-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/configuration/init-command#invalid-version","content":"**Cause**: the version (from `--set-version` or `SKILL.md`) is not valid semver.\n**Solution**: use a semver string such as `1.0.0`."},"490":{"id":"/configuration/init-command-80","page_id":"/configuration/init-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/configuration/init-command#permission-denied","content":"**Cause**: the current directory is not writable.\n**Solution**: fix permissions or run in a directory where you have write access."},"491":{"id":"/configuration/init-command-81","page_id":"/configuration/init-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/configuration/init-command#next-steps-after-init","content":"**Add skills**: `fastskill skill add <skill-id>` (registry, Git, or local path)."},"492":{"id":"/configuration/init-command-82","page_id":"/configuration/init-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/configuration/init-command#next-steps-after-init","content":"**Install from the manifest**: `fastskill project install`."},"493":{"id":"/configuration/init-command-83","page_id":"/configuration/init-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/configuration/init-command#next-steps-after-init","content":"**Index for search**: `fastskill index rebuild` (requires `OPENAI_API_KEY`)."},"494":{"id":"/configuration/init-command-84","page_id":"/configuration/init-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/configuration/init-command#next-steps-after-init","content":"**Search**: `fastskill skill search \"your query\"`."},"495":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"page","content":"Bundle commands","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Share with teams"],"tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command"},"496":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-0","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","content":"Build, install, update, restore, and customize self-contained team skill bundles."},"497":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-1","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#bundle-commands","content":"`bundle` commands"},"498":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-2","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#build-a-bundle","content":"Build a bundle"},"499":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-3","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"Install and inspect"},"500":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-4","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#update-a-bundle","content":"Update a bundle"},"501":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-5","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#remove-a-bundle","content":"Remove a bundle"},"502":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-6","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"Personal overrides"},"503":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-7","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#bundle-commands","content":"Bundles turn a selected team setup into one versioned ZIP. The artifact contains the selected\nskills, their installed dependency closure, resource files, and content digests. A recipient can\ninstall it without access to the original repositories."},"504":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-8","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#build-a-bundle","content":"Complete the quickstart, then add this declaration to that project's\nexisting `skill-project.toml`. Keep its `[dependencies]` and `[tool.fastskill]` sections."},"505":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-9","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#build-a-bundle","content":"Every bundle member must also appear in `[dependencies]`. The installed member version must\nsatisfy that declaration. FastSkill stops before writing an artifact when a declared member is\nmissing, has invalid frontmatter, or has a different version."},"506":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-10","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#build-a-bundle","content":"Build the release:"},"507":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-11","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#build-a-bundle","content":"The result is `dist/notes-team-1.0.0.zip`. Its embedded identity, version, membership, and\ndigests are authoritative, so renaming the download does not change the release."},"508":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-12","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"In a second project initialized with `project init --yes --skills-dir .claude/skills`,\ninstall the artifact with `bundle add`. Replace the local path with the artifact you\nbuilt. The HTTPS URL below is an example for an artifact hosted by your team:"},"509":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-13","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"Installation copies the artifact into `.fastskill/bundles/`, adds its declaration to\n`skill-project.toml`, and records the exact release and members in `skills.lock`."},"510":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-14","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"Commit these files when teammates and CI need the same setup:"},"511":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-15","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"Then restore the exact locked release:"},"512":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-16","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"`--lock` uses the bundle artifact, version, digest, and membership recorded in `skills.lock`.\nIt does not switch to a different release if the manifest has drifted. `--offline` additionally\nguarantees that restore does not contact a repository or embedding provider."},"513":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-17","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#update-a-bundle","content":"Bundle updates are explicit. After building version `1.1.0` of your bundle, preview\nand apply that replacement:"},"514":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-18","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#update-a-bundle","content":"FastSkill checks the new artifact, shared ownership, local modifications, and release immutability\nbefore it changes installed members. The preview runs the same validation as apply and reports\npolicy-only changes, such as a member becoming non-overridable, even when its bytes are unchanged."},"515":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-19","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#remove-a-bundle","content":"Remove the bundle identity and the members that have no other owner:"},"516":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-20","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#remove-a-bundle","content":"Removing a direct declaration detaches that owner. FastSkill retains the installed member while a\nbundle or another dependency root still requires it. An ID that is only a transitive requirement\ncannot be removed directly; the error names the roots that require it. A member is deleted only\nafter its final direct, transitive, bundle, and override owner is gone."},"517":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-21","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"An edited installed file is not an approved override. Put the customized skill in a separate\ndirectory and declare it explicitly. Every installed bundle that owns the skill must mark the\nmember as `overridable = true`."},"518":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-22","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"`fastskill project install` and `fastskill project install --lock` restore valid personal overrides after\nbundle members. Updates stop when a new bundle policy no longer permits an existing override."},"519":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-23","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"Return to the packaged member and clear the override records in one operation:"},"520":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-24","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"Reset is blocked if retained bundles disagree on the packaged bytes or if the installed member has\nuntracked edits. Removing the last bundle owner of a personal replacement keeps that replacement\nas an individual requirement instead of deleting it. FastSkill validates the replacement's complete\ndependency closure first; bundle removal is blocked if that closure cannot be retained."},"521":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-25","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"Every bundle action except `bundle list` changes files. The MCP server hides and refuses these\ntools unless it starts with `fastskill mcp serve --enable-write`."},"522":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"page","content":"cache Command","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","CLI commands","Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command"},"523":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-0","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command","content":"Inspect and reclaim the on-disk skill content cache with fastskill cache."},"524":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-1","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#cache-command","content":"cache Command"},"525":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-2","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#usage","content":"Usage"},"526":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-3","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#subcommands","content":"Subcommands"},"527":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-4","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"info"},"528":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-5","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"clean"},"529":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-6","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#when-to-run-it","content":"When to run it"},"530":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-7","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#see-also","content":"See Also"},"531":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-8","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#cache-command","content":"Inspect and reclaim the on-disk cache that `skill add`, `project install`, and `skill update` use so a skill's\ncontent is fetched once per machine instead of once per project."},"532":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-9","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#cache-command","content":"Every git, registry, or local skill fetch is checked against this cache before touching the\nnetwork again. `fastskill cache` is how to see what has accumulated there and reclaim disk\nspace -- fastskill never evicts cache entries on its own."},"533":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-10","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"Show the cache location plus entry counts and disk usage, broken down by source kind (git,\nregistry, or local)."},"534":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-11","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"**Example output**:"},"535":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-12","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"**Options**:"},"536":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-13","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"`--format <table|json>`: Output format (default: table)"},"537":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-14","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"`--json`: Shorthand for `--format json` (mutually exclusive with `--format`)"},"538":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-15","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"Remove cached skill content and print how many bytes were reclaimed."},"539":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-16","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"**Options**:"},"540":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-17","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"`--source <git|registry|local>`: Limit cleaning to one source kind (default: all)"},"541":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-18","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"`--json`: Print the result as JSON instead of a summary line"},"542":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-19","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"**What it removes**: Only cached skill content -- the record of what a repository currently\nadvertises (what `repo refresh` writes) is left alone, so `repo refresh` output stays valid\nafter a clean. There is nothing to undo: the next `skill add`/`project install`/`skill update` that needs a removed\nentry re-fetches it from its original source."},"543":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-20","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"**Safe with other fastskill processes running**: `clean` never removes an entry another process\nis mid-write on, and every write elsewhere is atomic. In the worst case, a fetch running at the\nexact moment of a clean simply re-fetches -- it never sees partial or corrupted content."},"544":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-21","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#when-to-run-it","content":"**`cache info`**: Before a `clean`, to see what is actually taking up space, or when disk\nusage seems higher than expected."},"545":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-22","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#when-to-run-it","content":"**`cache clean`**: To reclaim disk space after finishing with skills from a source no longer\nin use, or as routine cleanup on a machine used for many short-lived projects."},"546":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-23","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#see-also","content":"`repo` commands -- refresh what a repository advertises\n(`repo refresh`), independent of the content cache `cache` manages"},"547":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-24","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#see-also","content":"Install Command -- installs that hit this cache"},"548":{"id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","page_id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","type":"page","content":"Discover and inspect skills","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","CLI commands","Sources and distribution"],"tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands"},"549":{"id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands-0","page_id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","content":"Find a catalog result, inspect its origin, and install it explicitly."},"550":{"id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands-1","page_id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands#search-installed-skills","content":"Search installed skills"},"551":{"id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands-2","page_id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands#search-a-catalog","content":"Search a catalog"},"552":{"id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands-3","page_id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","content":"Complete the quickstart for local skills, or configure a real\ncatalog. Examples below use placeholder repository and skill IDs."},"553":{"id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands-4","page_id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands#search-installed-skills","content":"Local keyword search needs no API key. Semantic search is optional and requires an\nindex and embedding provider."},"554":{"id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands-5","page_id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands#search-a-catalog","content":"Remote search is the default when `--local` is absent. Results identify the\ncanonical skill ID, repository, version, and installation command. Empty catalogs,\nmissing configuration, and partial failures are distinct outcomes; inspect both\nJSON diagnostics and exit status."},"555":{"id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands-6","page_id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands#search-a-catalog","content":"See search reference for filters and output formats,\nand repository reference for catalog operations."},"556":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"page","content":"eval Command","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","CLI commands","Quality"],"tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command"},"557":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-0","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command","content":"Validate, run, report, and score skill evaluation suites defined in skill-project.toml."},"558":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-1","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#overview","content":"Overview"},"559":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-2","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#usage","content":"Usage"},"560":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-3","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"eval validate"},"561":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-4","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"eval run"},"562":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-5","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#environment-isolation","content":"Environment isolation"},"563":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-6","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"eval judge"},"564":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-7","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-report","content":"eval report"},"565":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-8","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-score","content":"eval score"},"566":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-9","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-scorecard","content":"eval scorecard"},"567":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-10","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-metrics-file","content":"The metrics file"},"568":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-11","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"Identity: what the numbers are about"},"569":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-12","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-json-document","content":"The JSON document"},"570":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-13","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-html-report","content":"The HTML report"},"571":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-14","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#what-is-excluded-and-why","content":"What is excluded, and why"},"572":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-15","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#see-also","content":"See also"},"573":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-16","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#overview","content":"`fastskill eval` runs skill quality checks using prompts and rubrics under `[tool.fastskill.eval]` in `skill-project.toml`. Subcommands are `validate`, `run`, `judge`, `report`, `score`, and `scorecard`."},"574":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-17","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#overview","content":"`eval run` requires an agent on `PATH` for the chosen `--agent` key. Known keys are `aikit`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `gemini`, and `pi`. A key is accepted only when its CLI is detected on the current machine, so a typo and an uninstalled agent both error with `RUNTIME_UNKNOWN_ID`, which lists what was detected. Use `eval validate --agent <key>` or `--all` to verify availability."},"575":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-18","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Checks eval configuration and files (optional agent presence check)."},"576":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-19","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Option"},"577":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-20","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Description"},"578":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-21","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`--agent <AGENT>`"},"579":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-22","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Verify the given agent(s) are available; repeatable. Mutually exclusive with `--all`"},"580":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-23","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`--all`"},"581":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-24","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Verify availability of every installed agent. Mutually exclusive with `--agent`"},"582":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-25","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`--model <MODEL>`"},"583":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-26","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"The model `eval run` will target; a judge declaring the same one is reported as self-preference"},"584":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-27","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`--format <FORMAT>`"},"585":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-28","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`table` or `json` only (eval does not support `grid`/`xml`)"},"586":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-29","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`--json`"},"587":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-30","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Shorthand for `--format json`"},"588":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-31","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Every `[[judge]]` in the checks file is validated from file content alone, so validate gives the same answer on a laptop and in CI. Errors: no resolvable `model`; neither or both of `prompt` / `prompt_file` (likewise for the system and retry pairs); an unknown `{{variable}}`; a `cases` id matching no case; duplicate criterion names; `scale` below 2; `min_score` outside `[0, 1]`; a prompt that never renders `{{output_contract}}`; any unknown key. Warnings: a prompt without `{{rubric}}`, and a judge sharing `--model`. Endpoint reachability and API keys are not checked here — judging checks those before its first request."},"589":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-32","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"With `--agent` or `--all`, both outputs report each selected agent:\nthe table prints one `agent '<key>': available|unavailable` line per agent, and the JSON document carries an `agents` object keyed by agent id (`{\"agents\": {\"claude\": true}}`). An unavailable agent is an error unless `fail_on_missing_agent = false` is set in the eval config."},"590":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-33","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Runs eval cases against an agent; writes artifacts under `--output-dir`."},"591":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-34","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`--agent <key>` (repeatable) and `--all` are mutually exclusive — passing both errors with `RUNTIME_CONFLICTING_FLAGS`. `eval run` requires one of them (passing neither errors with `RUNTIME_NO_SELECTION`)."},"592":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-35","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Option"},"593":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-36","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Description"},"594":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-37","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`--agent <AGENT>`"},"595":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-38","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Agent key(s) to run; repeatable. Required unless `--all` is given"},"596":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-39","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`--all`"},"597":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-40","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Run against all installed agents. Mutually exclusive with `--agent`"},"598":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-41","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`--output-dir <DIR>`"},"599":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-42","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"**Required.** Directory for run output"},"600":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-43","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`--model <MODEL>`"},"601":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-44","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Optional model override passed to the agent"},"602":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-45","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`--case <ID>`"},"603":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-46","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Run only this case id"},"604":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-47","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`--tag <TAG>`"},"605":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-48","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Run only cases with this tag"},"606":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-49","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`--format <FORMAT>`"},"607":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-50","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`table` or `json` only"},"608":{"id":"/cli-reference/