s the judge tier sees exactly what it saw before. Judging the same run twice asks nothing — a trial whose latest judgment carries the same request identity is skipped unless `--rejudge`."},"650":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-93","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"A trial that errored is never judged: there is no answer to score, and it is reported as skipped rather than as a zero. A judge that could not produce a judgment exits the command non-zero even under `--no-fail`, because a missing measurement must not be reported as a score."},"651":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-94","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-report","content":"Summarizes a completed run directory."},"652":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-95","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-report","content":"Option"},"653":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-96","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-report","content":"Description"},"654":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-97","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-report","content":"`--run-dir <DIR>`"},"655":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-98","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-report","content":"**Required.** The per-agent run directory — `<output-dir>/<timestamp>/<agent>`, the one that holds `summary.json`"},"656":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-99","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-report","content":"`--format <FORMAT>`"},"657":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-100","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-