tent":"Passes if `path` exists under the case's working directory — the case's scratch workspace under the default isolation (plus `workspace_subdir` when set), or the project root under `--no-isolation`."},"2191":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-159","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Field"},"2192":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-160","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Type"},"2193":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-161","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Required"},"2194":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-162","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Default"},"2195":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-163","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`limit`"},"2196":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-164","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"integer"},"2197":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-165","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"yes"},"2198":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-166","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"—"},"2199":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-167","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`required`"},"2200":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-168","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"bool"},"2201":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-169","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"no"},"2202":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-170","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`true`"},"2203":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-171","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Passes if the number of **tool invocations** the agent made is `<= limit`."},"2204":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-172","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"A tool invocation is a structured `tool_use` trace event, plus any `raw_json` trace line — the\nlatter covers backends that still emit tool calls as raw JSON instead of decoded tool events.\nAssistant text output, token-usage events, and unmodelled SDK event variants are **not** counted."},"2205":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-173","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Results use `\"check_name\": \"max_tool_calls\"`. The per-case artifact field counting\nthese events is `command_count`."},"2206":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-174","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Every check type accepts `required` (default `true`). Setting `required = false` makes the check **advisory**: it still runs, and its result still appears in the run artifacts with its own `passed` value, but a failure does not fail the case."},"2207":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-175","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Use it for signal you want visible in reports without gating the suite on it."},"2208":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-176","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"No `checks` file configured (or it loads zero explicit checks): the case still receives the required trigger expectation generated from `should_trigger`."},"2209":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-177","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"Any checks loaded: the case **passes** only if every **required** check's `passed` is `true`. Checks marked `required = false` are reported but never fail the case. Among required checks there is no partial credit and no threshold — they are all-or-nothing per case."},"2210":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-178","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"A case whose checks are **all** advisory (`required = false`) has nothing that can fail it, so it passes as long as it does not time out. That is intentional, but it means an all-optional `checks.toml` is not a safety net."},"2211":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-179","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"A trial that times out is always `error`, independent of checks."},"2212":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-180","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"Across trials, `pass_threshold` decides the case's aggregated status: pass rate across trials must be `>= pass_threshold`."},"2213":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-181","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"Once the manifest, CSV, and checks file exist:"},"2214":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-182","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"`--output-dir` is **required** on `fastskill eval run` — there is no default. Omitting it fails argument parsing before anything else runs:"},"2215":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-183","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"`--agent <key>` (repeatable) and `--all` are mutually exclusive on both `eval run` and `eval validate` — passing both errors with `RUNTIME_CONFLICTING_FLAGS`. `eval run` additionally requires one of them (passing neither errors with `RUNTIME_NO_SELECTION`); on `eval validate` both are optional — omit them to validate config without checking any agent's availability."},"2216":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-184","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"See Run evals for the full day-to-day command set, artifact layout, and CI gating pattern."},"2217":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-185","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"`[tool.fastskill.eval]` present with a `prompts` path that resolves."},"2218":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-186","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Prompts CSV has `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger` headers (plus `tags` / `workspace_subdir` if you use them)."},"2219":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-187","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Each `should_trigger` value reflects the required consultation/non-consultation expectation; explicit `skill_invoked` checks do not contradict it."},"2220":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-188","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Outcome correctness is measured separately where consultation alone is insufficient."},"2221":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-189","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"`fastskill eval validate --all` passes and lists the agent you intend to run against as available."},"2222":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-190","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Output directory convention agreed for `--output-dir` (local + CI)."},"2223":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-191","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"Run evals"},"2224":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-192","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"Cluster analysis"},"2225":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-193","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"eval command"},"2226":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"page","content":"Advanced Patterns","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","Workflow examples"],"tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns"},"2227":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-0","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns","content":"Analyze overlap, optimize skills, filter project groups, and manage editable and global skills."},"2228":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-1","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#overview","content":"Overview"},"2229":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-2","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Find duplicate and 