":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#start-with-skillmd","content":"The standard validator expects a lowercase name of 1–64 characters using letters,\ndigits, and single separating hyphens. The description must be nonempty and at most\n1024 characters. Name and description help an agent decide when to load the skill."},"3237":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-5","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#start-with-skillmd","content":"FastSkill derives identity from the skill metadata/name and uses a semantic version\nwhen resolving or packaging skills. Version metadata is optional for a minimal skill;\nFastSkill defaults an unspecified version to `1.0.0`. Set `metadata.version`\nexplicitly for a skill you distribute."},"3238":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-6","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#validate-installation-and-state","content":"After creating the source above, add it from a configured project:"},"3239":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-7","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#validate-installation-and-state","content":"Installation validates metadata and source contents. Reconciliation checks desired\nconstraints, locked facts, dependency ownership, and installed content. Editable\nlocal sources are reported as mutable rather than digest-verified."},"3240":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-8","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#validate-installation-and-state","content":"A successful structural check does not prove that instructions are safe or useful.\nReview scripts and resources, then use evals to measure\nbehavior on representative tasks. See reconciliation\nfor missing, changed, conflicting, and unverifiable installations."},"3241":{"id":"/testing/debugging","page_id":"/testi