ould_trigger` affects pass/fail.** The engine creates an implicit required `skill_invoked` check for each case, with `expected` equal to the CSV value. An explicit `skill_invoked` check that applies to the case replaces the implicit one; `eval validate` rejects a contradictory polarity. Therefore `false` tests non-consultation and `true` tests consultation, subject to the selected backend's observability."],[2094,"**`true`**"],[1285,"**100 skills**: \\~$0.001 (less than 1 cent)"],[2601,"**A new version is written only when a step is accepted**, so version numbers count\n*accepted steps*, not steps. Once any step has been rejected they no longer line up with\nstep indices: if step 0 is rejected and step 1 accepted, step 1's diff is\n`skill_v0000.md → skill_v0001.md`, not `v0001 → v0002`."],[2890,"**Access Control**: Registry access is controlled by authentication"],[491,"**Add skills**: `fastskill skill add <skill-id>` (registry, Git, or local path)."],[734,"**Advisory judge rows.** A `judge:<name>` row for a judge that does not gate never moves a `check_rate`. It is reported by the `judge_score` metric that names the judge."],[1267,"**API Key Issues**: Check `OPENAI_API_KEY` environment variable"],[2891,"**Audit Trail**: Publishing history is maintained automatically"],[224,"**Authors**: init, validate, eval, and ship skills via the platform."],[2800,"**Automatic rebuilding keeps the index fresh.** After `skill add`, `project install`,\n`skill update`, or `skill remove`, FastSkill\nreindexes automatically (unless `auto_reindex = false` or `--no-reindex`, and only when an\nembedding provider is available), so `resolve` reflects the current skill set."],[227,"**Automation**: `project install --lock` and reproducible installs in CI."],[1284,"**Average skill**: \\~500 tokens"],[1389,"**Behavior**:"],[706,"**Benchmark**"],[2888,"**Blob Storage**: Artifacts are stored securely with checksum verification"],[1971,"**Case-based evals** with `fastskill eval` to test expected 